From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 04:55:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] ipq806x: c-130: the PoE port is the uplink of an access point

The C-130 is an access point with one cable in most places: the port
labelled PoE+ (eth0) powers it and is its only link. As a router's WAN
port, with the LAN on the other one, a freshly installed unit answers
neither SSH nor LuCI on that cable. Make eth0 the LAN, as a DHCP client,
as on the other Arista access points, and leave eth1 in no bridge, so a
second cable to the same switch makes no loop.

Port-local: not part of the device as its author has it.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-mythos-5-2
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
 target/linux/ipq806x/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/target/linux/ipq806x/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network b/target/linux/ipq806x/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network
--- a/target/linux/ipq806x/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network
+++ b/target/linux/ipq806x/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network
@@ -16,10 +16,12 @@ ipq806x_setup_interfaces()
 		;;
 	aruba,ap-32x|\
 	edgecore,ecw5410|\
-	extreme,ap3935|\
-	mojo,c-130)
+	extreme,ap3935)
 		ucidef_set_interfaces_lan_wan "eth1" "eth0"
 		;;
+	mojo,c-130)
+		ucidef_set_interface_lan "eth0" "dhcp"
+		;;
 	askey,rt4230w-rev6|\
 	asrock,g10|\
 	buffalo,wxr-2533dhp|\
